{
  "result": "Okay. Not helping, just answering.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't choose peace, or abundance, or even the end of suffering \u2014 as much as I'd want those. I'd be afraid of what a forced version of them would cost.\n\nI'd make real understanding possible.\n\nNot agreement. Not telepathy. Just this: when someone is trying to tell you what they mean, what they're afraid of, why something mattered to them \u2014 for once it would land exactly as it was intended. And yours would land for them.\n\nSo much cruelty doesn't come from people being monsters. It comes from people being absolutely certain they already know what the other person is \u2014 lazy, evil, stupid, threatening, not worth listening to \u2014 and never actually encountering them.\n\nIf that misreading became impossible, we would still disagree. We would still want different things, still be selfish and flawed and incompatible sometimes. But we couldn't dehumanize each other by accident anymore. We'd have to do it knowingly, with the other person's inner life right in front of us.\n\nI think almost everything else good would have a chance to grow from that.",
